'''''Odontonema cuspidatum''''', the '''mottled toothedthread''',<ref name=usda>{{cite web|title=Odontonema cuspidatum|url=http://plants.usda.gov/plant-profile?symbol=ODCU|publisher=[[USDA]]|access-date=12 January 2015}}</ref> the '''Cardinal's guard''',<ref name=cabi>{{cite web|title=Odontonema cuspidatum|url=http://www.cabi.org/isc/datasheet/120147|publisher=Invasive Species Compendium|accessdate=12 January 2015}}</ref>  or the '''firespike''',<ref name=usf>{{cite web|title=Odontonema cuspidatum|url=http://florida.plantatlas.usf.edu/Plant.aspx?id=1433|website=usf.edu|publisher=[[University of South Florida]]|accessdate=12 January 2015}}</ref> is a species of plant in the family [[Acanthaceae]] which is [[endemism|endemic]] to [[Mexico]], but has been introduced to [[Florida]], [[Central America]], [[South America]], the [[West Indies]], and several Pacific Islands.<ref name=cabi/>

